# 28. Simulation Philosophy

The simulator should use the fitted structural model.

It should **never** fit auxiliary regressions.

Every prediction should be generated from the structural demand equation.

The simulator should evaluate customer-level probabilities first.

Aggregation occurs afterward.

This is essential because

[
E[\Lambda(Z)]
\neq
\Lambda(E[Z]).
]

---

