# 30. Schedule-Based Counterfactuals

A scalar price curve ignores the heterogeneous pricing schedule.

Also support evaluation of complete pricing schedules.

Each candidate schedule supplies

new base price,

binary increments,

count increments.

Reconstruct the induced conditional price distribution using the estimated latent form model.

Then evaluate demand under the new schedule.

This preserves heterogeneous prices across customers.

---

# 31. Additive Price Shifts

Support

[
P^{cf}
======

P+\delta.
]

This permits simple pricing analyses without rebuilding the pricing schedule.

Return

conversion,

quantity,

revenue,

relative to the baseline.

---

# 32. Revenue

Uniform-price revenue

is

[
R(p)
====

pQ(p).
]

Schedule-level revenue must instead integrate

realized price

times

completion probability

over the complete conditional price distribution.

Never replace this calculation by

average price

times

average conversion.

---

# 33. Revenue Optimization

Support

grid search,

bounded one-dimensional optimization,

evaluation of candidate pricing schedules.

Return

best price,

best revenue,

best conversion,

revenue relative to baseline.

Grid search should be the default.

