# 45. Negative Binomial Extension

The first production implementation should use Poisson.

The architecture should nevertheless allow replacement of the count family.

The negative-binomial extension changes only

the count-form likelihood,

the conditional count-price recursion.

The remainder of the estimator

demand,

latent factor,

quadrature,

binary convolution,

simulation,

counterfactual engine,

diagnostics,

should remain unchanged.

Implement the extension only after

the Poisson model passes all validation tests

and

simulation recovers known parameters.

